+// Cloudflare runs of the latency and where-it-runs measurements, on the owner's account. Nothing here runs without
+// CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID.
+//   bun bench/cloud.ts deploy <target>                 uploads the bundle Miniflare runs (same bytes; BENCH_PROBE picks the
+//                                                      probe bundle) as Worker durable-bench-<target>[-probe-<mode>]
+//   bun bench/cloud.ts run <target> <url> [sizes...]   one Durable Object per size and sample; seeds through /seed, waits
+//                                                      out the eviction window, then times /wake and the turns at the client
+// Latency lines go to results/cloudflare.jsonl (durable-bench format plus `floor`, the median Worker-only round trip of
+// the same run). With BENCH_PROBE=count|time the run reads /probe after every request, takes each request's CPU time from
+// `wrangler tail` (the Worker invocation plus the Durable Object invocations it caused), and writes probe lines with
+// host "cloudflare" to results/cloudflare-probe.jsonl. The isolate heap is not observable on Cloudflare, so those lines
